WEBVTT

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:08.280
Don't think you've
avoided talking about
the principal's office.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.400
Your father and I
are still gonna
discuss it.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.320
I'm not the only kid
who's been sent to
the office.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.240
Other kids don't
have superpowers.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.600
Now, it's
perfectly normal...

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.400
What do you know
about normal?

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:21.880
What does anyone
in this family know
about normal?

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.240
Now, wait a minute,
young lady.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:25.720
We act normal.
I wanna be normal.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.560
The only normal one
is Jack-Jack,

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:29.680
and he's not even
toilet trained.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.240
(LAUGHING)

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.000
Lucky.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:35.560
I meant
about being normal.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.400
(LAUGHTER)

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:39.960
LUCIUS: So now
I'm in deep trouble.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.320
I mean, one more jolt
of this death ray
and I'm an epitaph.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.240
Somehow I managed
to find cover.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:46.880
What does Baron
Von Ruthless do?

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:47.960
He starts monologuing.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:49.520
He starts monologuing.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.520
He starts this prepared
speech about how feeble
I am compared to him.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.520
How inevitable
my defeat is,

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.920
the world
will soon be his.
Yada, yada, yada.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.280
Yammering.
Yammering.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:02.640
I mean, the guy
has me on a platter,
and he won't shut up.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:05.040
RADIO: Municiberg,
we have a 23-56...

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:06.600
23-56, what is that?

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:08.640
Robbery?
This is just sad.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:10.920
Want to catch a robber?
No.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.280
Tell you the truth,
I'd rather go bowling.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:17.840
Look, what if we actually
did what our wives think
we're doing?

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:19.480
Just to shake things up.

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:24.200
MIRAGE: He's not alone.
The fat guy's still
with him.

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:26.680
They're just talking.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:28.680
What are we
doing here?

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:29.840
Protecting people.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:30.960
Nobody asked us.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:32.200
You need an invitation?

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:35.880
I'd like one, yes.
We keep sneaking out
to do this, and...

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:37.480
You remember Gazerbeam?

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.400
There was something
in the paper.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:41.400
He had trouble
with civilian life.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:42.720
When did you see him?

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:46.320
I don't see anyone
from the old days.
Just you.

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.640
And we're pushing
our luck as it is.
Come on.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.480
It was fun the first time,
but if we keep doing this...

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:53.640
RADIO: We have
a report on a fire...

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:55.080
A fire. We're close!

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:56.480
(YELLING) Yeah, baby!

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:57.800
We're gonna get caught.

00:01:58.040 --> 00:01:59.240
(HOOTING)

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.240
BOB: Fire! Yeah!

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:12.360
LUCIUS:
Is that everybody?

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:13.520
BOB: Yeah.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.600
It better be.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:18.280
Can't you put this out?

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:21.680
I can't lay down
a layer thick enough!
It's evaporating too fast!

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:23.840
What's that mean?
It means it's hot.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:25.120
I'm dehydrated, Bob.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.280
You're out of ice?

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:28.720
You can't run out.
You can use water
in the air.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:30.600
There is no water
in this air!

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:32.600
What's your excuse,
run out of muscle?

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:35.600
I can't smash walls.
The building's
getting weaker.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:37.000
It's gonna come down
on top of us.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:38.840
I wanted to go bowling!

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:45.240
All right!
Stay right on my tail!
This is gonna get hot!

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.320
(COUGHING, MOANING)

00:02:58.120 --> 00:02:59.240
BOB: Yeah.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:00.840
(COUGHING)

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.400
Uh-oh.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:06.040
Oh, good.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:08.240
(ALARM SOUNDS)
(GROANS)

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:09.720
That ain't right.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.480
We look like
incompetent bad guys!

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.560
You can get water
out of the air.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:17.160
Freeze!

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.080
Freeze!

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:24.480
I'm thirsty.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:25.960
I said freeze!

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:28.920
I'm just getting a drink.

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:34.520
You've had your
drink. Now...

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:37.920
I know. I know. Freeze.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:40.520
(POLICE RADIO CHATTER)

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.520
Police officers!

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:56.360
LUCIUS: That was
way too close.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:59.160
We are not
doing that again.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:04.720
(OVER RADIO) Verify
you want to switch
targets? Over.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:05.840
Trust me.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:08.240
This is the one
he's been looking for.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:11.560
(KEYS JINGLING)

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:13.040
(HUMMING)

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:36.280
I thought you'd
be back by 11:00.

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:37.640
I said
I'd be back later.

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:40.320
I assumed you'd be
back later. If you
came back at all,

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:41.560
you'd be "back later".

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:44.400
Well, I'm back, okay?

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:53.160
Is this rubble?

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:55.520
(WITH MOUTH FULL)
It was just
a little workout.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:56.680
Just to stay loose.

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:58.520
You know how
I feel about that.

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:00.360
Darn you!
We can't blow
cover again.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:02.320
The building was
coming down anyway.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.600
What?

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:05.280
You knocked down
a building?

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:08.360
It was on fire.
Structurally unsound.
It was coming down.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:10.840
Have you been listening
to the police scanner again?

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:12.520
I performed
a public service.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:13.960
You act like
that's a bad thing.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.440
It is a bad thing, Bob!

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:17.360
Uprooting our
family again,

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.680
so you can relive
the glory days
is a bad thing.

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:22.680
It's better
than acting like
they didn't happen!

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:25.600
Yes! They happened!
But this, our family,

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.520
is what's
happening now, Bob.

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:29.160
And you are
missing this!

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:32.360
I can't believe
you don't want to go to
your own son's graduation.

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:35.480
It's not a graduation.
He's moving from fourth
to fifth grade.

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:37.640
It's a ceremony!
It's psychotic!

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:40.480
They keep creating new ways
to celebrate mediocrity

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:42.480
but if someone
is exceptional...

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:44.800
This is not
about you, Bob.
It's about Dash.

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:46.400
You want to do
something for Dash?

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:47.720
Let him
actually compete.

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:48.960
Let him go out
for sports!

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:50.640
I will not be
made the enemy!

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:53.240
You know why
we can't do that.
Because he'd be great.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:55.480
This is not about you!

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:01.120
All right, Dash.
I know you're listening.
Come on out.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.480
Vi? You, too,
young lady.

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:05.960
Come on.
Come on out.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:09.280
It's okay, kids.
We're just having
a discussion.

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:11.160
VIOLET:
Pretty loud discussion.

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:12.400
But that's okay.

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:14.840
What's important
is that Mommy
and I are a team.

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:19.680
We're united, uh,
against forces of...

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:20.760
Pigheadedness?

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:22.240
I was gonna say evil.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:23.440
We're sorry
we woke you.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:26.200
Everything's okay.
Go back to bed.
It's late.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:28.040
Good night, Mom.
Night, Dad.
Good night.

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:31.600
In fact,
we should all
be in bed.

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:37.160
(SIGHS)

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:42.320
(CRICKETS CHIRPING,
DOG BARKS)

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:49.360
(ON PHONE) Request claim
on claim numbers 158183...

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:51.640
HUPH: Haven't
you got him yet?
Where is he?

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:54.720
PA: Mr. Huph would
like to talk to you
in his office.

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:56.880
Now?
Now.

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:01.880
(ANNOUNCEMENT ON PA)

